smells.EagerTest:
Extract the common JsonReader creation and beginArray() call into a private helper method, e.g.
```java
private JsonReader setupReader(String json) throws IOException {
    JsonReader r = new JsonReader(reader(json));
    r.beginArray();
    return r;
}
```
Then split the original test into four focused test methods, each covering a single malformed‑array scenario, and invoke the helper for setup. Each new test retains the same assertions (assertThat, assertThrows, assertStrictError) but isolates them, removing the eager‑test smell.

