smells.MysteryGuest:
Inject a JUnit 5 temporary directory into the test method with @TempDir and copy the HTML resource into that directory before parsing. Replace the direct call to `ParseTest.getFile(...)` with a call that reads the file from the injected temporary directory, e.g.
```java
@Test
public void testNewsHomepage(@TempDir File tempDir) throws IOException {
    File in = copyResourceToTempDir("/htmltests/news-com-au-home.html", tempDir);
    // …rest of test
}
```
This removes the hidden dependency on a class‑path resource location and makes the file handling explicit.

