smells.AssertionRoulette:
Add a descriptive message to every assert (except assertThat/assertThrows). Example changes: 
- assertFalse(StringUtil.isBlank(textNode.text())) → assertFalse("TextNode text should not be blank", StringUtil.isBlank(textNode.text()));
- assertEquals("One ", textNode.text()) → assertEquals("First TextNode text should be 'One '", "One ", textNode.text());
- assertEquals("One ", textNode.getWholeText()) → assertEquals("First TextNode wholeText should be 'One '", "One ", textNode.getWholeText());
- assertTrue(foundFirst) → assertTrue("At least one TextNode must be found", foundFirst);

smells.ConditionalTestLogic:
Extract the nested loops and the inner if‑logic into private helper methods. For example:
- private TextNode findFirstTextNode(Document doc) { /* iterate over doc.getAllElements() and return the first TextNode */ }
- private void assertTextNodeNotBlank(TextNode tn) { assertFalse("TextNode text should not be blank", StringUtil.isBlank(tn.text())); }
Then the test method only calls these helpers, removing complex control‑flow from the test body.

smells.EagerTest:
Separate the test into three focused test methods, each asserting a single logical concern, and extract the common document parsing into a shared private setup method. Example:
- private Document parseTestDocument() { return Jsoup.parse("<div>One <p>Two <p>Three"); }
- @Test public void testHasTextWhenIterating_NonBlank() { Document doc = parseTestDocument(); /* iterate and assertNotBlank */ }
- @Test public void testHasTextWhenIterating_FirstTextNode() { Document doc = parseTestDocument(); /* get first TextNode and assert its text */ }
- @Test public void testHasTextWhenIterating_FoundFirst() { Document doc = parseTestDocument(); /* verify foundFirst is true */ }

